bbcode_enabled = true
text = "
[b]Epstien Fuck Niggers[/b]

[b]Healthy[/b]
A patient with no detected illness or abnormal symptoms.
Symptoms:
• Normal temperature
• Normal blood pressure
• Normal breathing
• Normal heartbeat
• Clear saliva
• Normal eyes


[b]Viral Conjunctivitis[/b]
A viral infection of the eye that causes inflammation of the conjunctiva.
Symptoms:
• Pink/red eyes
• Mild fever
• Eye irritation
• Increased tearing


[b]Bacterial Pneumonia[/b]
A bacterial infection that causes inflammation and fluid buildup in the lungs.
Symptoms:
• High fever
• Green saliva/mucus
• Crackling lung sounds
• Rapid heartbeat
• Weakness


[b]Endocarditis[/b]
An infection of the inner lining of the heart that can disrupt normal heart function.
Symptoms:
• Fever
• Irregular heartbeat
• Abnormal lung sounds
• Fatigue
• Low energy


[b]Myocarditis[/b]
Inflammation of the heart muscle that can affect heartbeat and circulation.
Symptoms:
• Fever
• Irregular heartbeat
• Chest discomfort
• Fatigue
• Weakness


[b]Septic Shock[/b]
A severe infection response causing dangerous drops in blood pressure.
Symptoms:
• High fever
• Very low blood pressure
• Rapid heartbeat
• Weakness
• Confusion


[b]Anaphylaxis[/b]
A severe allergic reaction causing breathing difficulty and circulation problems.
Symptoms:
• Wheezing
• Low blood pressure



[b]Stimulant Overdose[/b]
A toxic reaction caused by excessive stimulant activity in the body.
Symptoms:
• Bloodshot eyes
• High blood pressure
• Extremely fast heartbeat
• Increased body temperature
• Agitation


[b]Opioid Overdose[/b]
A dangerous reaction caused by excessive opioid effects on the nervous system.
Symptoms:
• Abnormal eyes
• Slow heartbeat
• Low blood pressure
\\


[b]Hypothermia[/b]
A condition where the body temperature drops below normal levels.
Symptoms:
• Low body temperature
• Slow heartbeat
• Weakness
• Confusion
• Shivering


[b]Heat Stroke[/b]
A dangerous condition caused by extreme overheating of the body.
Symptoms:
• Very high temperature
• Fast heartbeat
• Strong heartbeat
• Confusion
• Weakness


[b]Heart Failure[/b]
A condition where the heart cannot pump blood effectively.
Symptoms:
• Crackling lung sounds
• Irregular heartbeat
• Shortness of breath
• Fatigue
• Weakness


[b]Atrial Fibrillation[/b]
An irregular heart rhythm caused by abnormal electrical activity in the heart.
Symptoms:
• Irregular heartbeat
• High blood pressure
• Rapid heartbeat
• Dizziness
• Fatigue


[b]Hypertension[/b]
A condition where blood pressure remains higher than normal.
Symptoms:
• High blood pressure
• Strong heartbeat
• Headache
• Dizziness
• Fatigue


[b]Seasonal Allergies[/b]
An immune reaction to airborne substances such as pollen.
Symptoms:
• Pink eyes
• Wheezing
• Sneezing
• Runny nose
• Eye irritation


[b]Viral Bronchitis[/b]
A viral infection causing inflammation of the airways.
Symptoms:
• Wheezing
• White saliva/mucus
• Mild fever
• Cough
• Chest discomfort


[b]Bacterial Bronchitis[/b]
A bacterial infection causing inflammation of the bronchial tubes.
Symptoms:
• Wheezing
• Green saliva/mucus
• Fever
• Cough
• Chest discomfort


[b]Bronchitis[/b]
Inflammation of the airways that affects breathing.
Symptoms:
• Wheezing
• Fever
• Cough
• Chest discomfort
• Fatigue


[b]Asthma[/b]
A condition where the airways narrow and make breathing difficult.
Symptoms:
• Wheezing
• Shortness of breath
• Chest tightness
• Difficulty breathing


[b]Tuberculosis[/b]
A bacterial infection that primarily affects the lungs.
Symptoms:
• Crackling lung sounds
• Green saliva/mucus
• Fever
• Persistent cough
• Weakness


[b]Allergic Conjunctivitis[/b]
An allergic reaction causing inflammation of the eyes.
Symptoms:
• Pink eyes
• Eye irritation
• Tearing
• Itching"
threaded = true

